## Phase 6: Handle LocalStorage Unavailable

**Issue**: Private browsing mode or disabled localStorage can cause errors.

**Solution**:
1. Wrap localStorage calls in try/catch
2. Fall back to session-only key storage or show warning

**Implementation**:
```javascript
function getKey() {
    try {
        var urlKey = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('key');
        if (urlKey) {
            localStorage.setItem('mad_key', urlKey);
            return urlKey;
        }
        return localStorage.getItem('mad_key') || '';
    } catch (e) {
        // localStorage unavailable
        return new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('key') || '';
    }
}

function saveKey() {
    try {
        localStorage.setItem('mad_key', k);
    } catch (e) {
        alert('LocalStorage unavailable. Key will not persist after closing browser.');
    }
    // ... rest
}

function logout() {
    try {
        localStorage.removeItem('mad_key');
    } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }
    // ...
}
```

