## Implementation Order

1. Phase 1 - Fix modal rendering (critical bug)
2. Phase 2 - Fix data leakage (security critical)
3. Phase 3 - Client page auth (security gap)
4. Phase 4 - Logout button (user request)
5. Phase 5 - Error feedback (UX improvement)
6. Phase 6 - LocalStorage fallback (edge case)
7. Phase 7 - WebSocket (if needed)
8. Phase 8 - HTMX endpoints (security)

---

## Files to Modify

1. `server/api.go` - Auth checks, data leakage fix, client page auth
2. `server/templates/index.html` - Modal placement, logout button, error display, JS functions
3. `server/templates/client.html` - Add key modal and auth check (or reuse from shared template)

---

## Test Scenarios

1. DashboardKey configured, no key in URL/localStorage → Modal appears, no data in page source
2. DashboardKey configured, valid key entered → Modal hidden, dashboard shows data
3. DashboardKey configured, invalid key entered → Error message shown
4. DashboardKey configured, logout clicked → Key cleared, modal appears
5. DashboardKey NOT configured → Modal never appears, no auth required
6. Client page without key → Modal appears, no data shown
7. localStorage unavailable → Works without persistence
8. Network error during validation → Allows save, lets server validate on next request"
}
